{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1944","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1944","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1944\",\"parent_revision\":\"c814c0ed0ea534237e9e4f84e40fe032da54ef87\",\"root_revision\":\"2417114212c5e3c50bc74d2808f993ebd4719abba679d7e1e661f74575f7ae43\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDate: 2026-05-02 | Claims checked: 6 | VERIFIED: 4 | REFUTED: 1 | INCONCLUSIVE: 1\\n\\nClaim 1: task_status_hook.py writes LastActivity on PostToolUse \u2014 VERIFIED. Source: task_status_hook.py line 899: sam_update_plan_fields(..., set_fields={\\\"last-activity\\\": timestamp}).\\n\\nClaim 2: Task.last_activity at models.py lines 150-154 \u2014 VERIFIED. Source: models.py 150-154: last_activity: datetime | None = Field(..., validation_alias=AliasChoices(\\\"last-activity\\\", \\\"last_activity\\\")).\\n\\nClaim 3: PlanStatus at models.py lines 522-535 with no stalled_tasks \u2014 VERIFIED. Source: models.py 522-535: 7-field model, no stalled_tasks field present.\\n\\nClaim 4: get_plan_status at query.py lines 372-411 \u2014 VERIFIED. Source: query.py line 372: def get_plan_status(plan_path: Path) -> PlanStatus.\\n\\nClaim 5: _sam_plan_status at server.py lines 323-338 \u2014 REFUTED. Lines 323-338 contain _sam_plan_list. Correct location: server.py lines 349-364. Resource table updated.\\n\\nClaim 6: No stall/stalled/stall_threshold refs in plugins/development-harness/ \u2014 INCONCLUSIVE. Consistent with all reads and backlog search. Direct grep not confirmed independently.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Add stalled-task detection using LastActivity timestamp to implementation_manager status\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Add stalled_tasks detection field to sam_plan status response using existing Task.last_activity timestamps.\\nConditions:\\n1. Task.last_activity field exists in Task model | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 verified at models.py lines 150-154\\n2. task_status_hook.py writes last-activity on PostToolUse events | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 verified at task_status_hook.py line 899\\n3. PlanStatus model exists and lacks stalled_tasks field | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 verified at models.py lines 522-535: 6-field model, no stalled_tasks field present\\n4. get_plan_status iterates all tasks and builds status counts | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 verified at query.py lines 372-411\\n5. _sam_plan_status entry point for status action | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 verified at server.py lines 349-364\\n6. Stall threshold value | Status: MISSING \u2014 no definition in item, codebase, or config\\n7. Threshold configurability | Status: MISSING \u2014 not specified (env var, plan field, or hardcoded)\\n8. Behavior for last_activity=None tasks | Status: MISSING \u2014 CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=minimal skips PostToolUse; include or exclude undefined\\n9. Scope: sam_plan ready as well as sam_plan status | Status: MISSING \u2014 item describes status only; stall detection also relevant to ready-task dispatch but not specified\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 4\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS** \u2014 the codebase provides all necessary hooks; four design decisions require human input before execution.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add stalled-task detection using lastactivity timestamp to implementation_manager status** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/abtop.md \u2014 pattern: SessionStatus enum (Thinking/Executing/Waiting/RateLimited/Done) for real-time agent state detection\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item title: add stalled-task detection to sam_plan status using LastActivity |\\n| Task.last_activity field | AVAILABLE | sam_schema/core/models.py lines 150-154 |\\n| LastActivity write path | AVAILABLE | task_status_hook.py line 899 |\\n| sam_plan status return shape | AVAILABLE | server.py _sam_plan_status() returns PlanStatus dict |\\n| get_plan_status compute layer | AVAILABLE | query.py lines 372-411 |\\n| Stall threshold definition | MISSING | No definition in item, codebase, or config |\\n| Threshold configurability | MISSING | Not specified |\\n| Behavior for last_activity=None | MISSING | CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=minimal skips PostToolUse |\\n| Scope: status vs ready | PARTIAL | Item says status; stall also relevant to ready \u2014 not specified |\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Create a SAM plan with at least one task in `in-progress` status.\\n2. Set the task's `last-activity` timestamp to a value older than the intended stall threshold (e.g., 2 hours ago).\\n3. Call `sam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"status\\\"}, plan=\\\"<plan_id>\\\")` via the MCP tool.\\n4. Observe the response \u2014 the `stalled_tasks` key is absent (the gap). The task that has been silent is not surfaced as stalled.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Stalled tasks are an invisible failure mode for the orchestrator. Without this signal, `/dh:execution` must either wait the full allowed time or kill agents blindly. Blocks the orchestrator recovery feature and degrades reliability of any long-running parallel dispatch. P1 is correct; this is not P0 only because the orchestrator can still function (with degraded reliability) without it.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen sam_plan status is called on a plan with in-progress tasks, the response includes a stalled_tasks field: a list of task IDs whose last_activity timestamp is older than the stall threshold and whose status is in-progress. Tasks with no last_activity set must be handled explicitly \u2014 either excluded, or treated as stalled from started time.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nsam_plan status response gains a stalled_tasks: list[str] field alongside existing by_status, ready_tasks, blocked_tasks, completion_pct. Detection logic lives in get_plan_status (query.py) or _sam_plan_status (server.py). PlanStatus in models.py gains the stalled_tasks field. stalled_tasks is a detection signal, not a new lifecycle state.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `sam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"status\\\"}, plan=\\\"P1\\\")` response contains a `stalled_tasks` key listing task IDs of in-progress tasks whose `last_activity` is older than the threshold.\\n2. `stalled_tasks` is an empty list `[]` when no in-progress task exceeds the threshold.\\n3. `stalled_tasks` is an empty list `[]` when no tasks are in-progress.\\n4. A task with `last_activity=None` and status `in-progress` does not raise an exception; its inclusion or exclusion from `stalled_tasks` is documented in a code comment or docstring.\\n5. The stall threshold is observable: either a named constant, an env var (e.g. `DH_STALL_THRESHOLD_MINUTES`), or a documented `sam_plan` parameter \u2014 not a magic number.\\n6. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` exits 0 after changes.\\n7. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/ -k stall -x` passes with tests covering: threshold exceeded fires detection, no stall returns empty list, no in-progress tasks returns empty list, None last_activity does not raise.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What duration defines a stalled task? Suggested default: 30 minutes. Is that correct?\\n- Should the threshold be configurable via env var (e.g. `DH_STALL_THRESHOLD_MINUTES`), a `sam_plan status` parameter, or a hardcoded named constant?\\n- Should tasks with `last_activity=None` (common when `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=minimal` is active, which skips PostToolUse) be included in `stalled_tasks` based on `started` time, or excluded entirely?\\n- Should `stalled_tasks` also appear in `sam_plan ready` output, or only `sam_plan status`?\\n- Should the prior grooming's candidate scope be included: a dedicated `implementation_manager.py stalled` CLI subcommand, `--threshold-minutes=N` CLI flag, and `last_activity_age_minutes` integer in the response? These were in the 2026-04-26 grooming notes but are not in the item description or acceptance criteria.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:implementation-manager |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Task.last_activity (lines 150-154), PlanStatus (lines 522-535) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py \u2014 get_plan_status (lines 372-411) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py \u2014 _sam_plan_status (lines 349-364) [corrected from prior 323-338] |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py \u2014 PostToolUse last-activity write (line 899) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: Any orchestrator recovery feature that needs to identify dead agents\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Stall threshold is undefined \u2014 required before execution.\\n- Behavior for last_activity=None tasks is undefined \u2014 required before execution.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall / Medium \u2014 PlanStatus gains one field; detection logic in get_plan_status is approximately 10-15 lines. Effort is Small if threshold is hardcoded and None tasks are excluded. Effort is Medium if threshold is configurable and last_activity=None edge cases are handled.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 documents PlanStatus shape indirectly via SAM pipeline description; update if stalled_tasks is promoted to a first-class dispatch signal\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_sam_plan_status` (lines 349-364) \u2014 returns `PlanStatus` dict; new field picked up automatically via model serialization\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::_sam_plan_ready` (lines 367-400) \u2014 calls `get_plan_status`; no direct change needed unless scope expands to include ready output\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 writes `last-activity` field (line 899); no change needed, already produces the data\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py::PlanStatus` \u2014 add `stalled_tasks: list[str]` field\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py::get_plan_status` \u2014 compute elapsed time since last_activity for in-progress tasks and populate stalled_tasks\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified (threshold value and configurability mechanism are design decisions gating execution)\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Status**: ALIGNMENT_CLEAN with one scope divergence noted.\\n\\nThe item consistently targets `sam_plan status` (the PlanStatus contract). The existing `get_plan_status` / `PlanStatus` / `_sam_plan_status` pipeline is a coherent stack with a single data contract \u2014 adding `stalled_tasks` to `PlanStatus` and computing it in `get_plan_status` is the architecturally correct insertion point, consistent with how `has_cycles`, `ready_tasks`, and `blocked_tasks` were added.\\n\\nThe prior grooming entry (2026-04-26 Measurable Signal section) introduced additional scope:\\n- A new CLI subcommand `implementation_manager.py stalled <project> <slug>`\\n- A `--threshold-minutes=N` CLI override parameter\\n- A `last_activity_age_minutes` integer in the response\\n- A `stall_threshold_minutes` field on the `Plan` model\\n\\nNone of these appear in the current item title, description, story, or acceptance criteria. These are CANDIDATE scope expansions, not confirmed requirements.\\n\\n**Recommendation**: present the candidate scope to the human for confirmation before including in the implementation plan. The core item (stalled_tasks field on PlanStatus, computed in get_plan_status) is well-scoped. The CLI subcommand and Plan-model field are separable additions.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 status output example must be updated to show `stalled_tasks` field\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] PlanStatus.stalled_tasks field added to models.py\\n- [ ] get_plan_status computes stall detection in query.py\\n- [ ] _sam_plan_status consumer tested end-to-end\\n- [ ] stall threshold defined and observable (constant, env var, or plan field)\\n- [ ] last_activity=None behavior documented and tested\\n- [ ] SKILL.md status output example updated\\n- [ ] pytest -k stall passes\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Producers**: models.py::PlanStatus (add stalled_tasks: list[str]); query.py::get_plan_status (compute elapsed time, populate stalled_tasks).\\n**Code \u2014 Consumers**: server.py::_sam_plan_status lines 349-364 (returns PlanStatus dict; new field auto-serialized); server.py::_sam_plan_ready (calls get_plan_status; no change unless scope expands to ready output).\\n**Code \u2014 Other References**: task_status_hook.py line 899 (writes last-activity; already functional, no change needed).\\n**Documentation**: skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md \u2014 status output example must show stalled_tasks field.\\n**Configuration / CI**: None identified (threshold value and configurability are unresolved design decisions).\\n**Agent Instructions**: plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 update if stalled_tasks becomes a first-class dispatch-recovery signal.\\n\\n**Systems Inventory**: models.py (PlanStatus data contract), query.py (compute layer), server.py (MCP entry point), task_status_hook.py (last-activity writer, no change needed), test files for PlanStatus/get_plan_status (need stall test cases).\\n\\n**Ecosystem Completeness Checklist**:\\n- [ ] PlanStatus.stalled_tasks field added to models.py\\n- [ ] get_plan_status computes stall detection in query.py\\n- [ ] _sam_plan_status consumer tested end-to-end\\n- [ ] Stall threshold defined and observable\\n- [ ] last_activity=None behavior documented and tested\\n- [ ] SKILL.md status output example updated\\n- [ ] uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/ -k stall passes\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nTask.last_activity is already populated by the PostToolUse hook (task_status_hook.py line 899). get_plan_status in query.py already iterates all tasks. The gap is that PlanStatus has no stalled_tasks field and get_plan_status does not compute elapsed time since last_activity.\\n\\nUnresolved design choices requiring human input before execution:\\n- Stall threshold value and whether it is configurable.\\n- Handling of last_activity=None (absent when CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=minimal is active).\\n- Whether stalled_tasks appears in sam_plan ready as well as sam_plan status.\\n\\nstalled_tasks must be a detection signal, not a new TaskStatus value \u2014 stalled is an observation, not a lifecycle transition.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n**Rationale**: The gap is not a traceable failure or surface fix \u2014 it is a missing feature requiring design decisions before execution. The stall threshold value, threshold configurability, None-task handling, and status-vs-ready scope are all open design choices with no prior art in the codebase. Four MISSING RT-ICA conditions confirm this classification.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: orchestrator running /dh:execution cannot distinguish active agents from dead ones \u2192 orchestrator gains a stalled_tasks signal enabling targeted recovery without blind killing or indefinite waiting\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an orchestrator running /dh:execution, when I call sam_plan status I need to see which in-progress tasks have been silent longer than a threshold so I can detect deadlocked or crashed agents and take recovery action without waiting indefinitely.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 domain model; PlanStatus is the data contract between query layer and server layer\\n- `sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 compute layer; get_plan_status iterates tasks and computes counts\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP entry point; _sam_plan_status surfaces PlanStatus to callers\\n- `task_status_hook.py` \u2014 hook that writes last-activity timestamps; already functional\\n- Test files for PlanStatus / get_plan_status \u2014 need new stall-detection test cases\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`implementation_manager.py status` output includes a `stalled_tasks: [...]` array enumerating every task where `status=IN_PROGRESS` AND `now - LastActivity > stall_threshold_minutes`. Default threshold = 15 minutes; readable from plan-level `stall_threshold_minutes` field on the `Plan` model in `sam_schema/core/models.py` or from a new top-level field in the plan YAML. New CLI subcommand `implementation_manager.py stalled <project> <slug>` returns only the stalled list (machine-parseable JSON). `ready-tasks` callers can decide to re-dispatch a stalled task to another agent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py status <project> <slug>` against a plan with one IN_PROGRESS task whose `LastActivity` is older than the threshold. Output JSON contains a `stalled_tasks` field with at least that task's `id` and a `last_activity_age_minutes` integer. Run with `--threshold-minutes=N` overrides the default. Field `stall_threshold_minutes` is present in `sam_schema/core/models.py` `Plan` class (search returns a non-zero match).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`task_status_hook.py` writes a `LastActivity` timestamp on every `Write|Edit|Bash` PostToolUse event (lines 15, 854, 930-933). `implementation_manager.py status` and `ready-tasks` commands report `in_progress`, `not_started`, `blocked`, `deferred`, `skipped` task counts (lines 1060-1067) but never inspect `LastActivity`. Grep of `plugins/development-harness/` for `stall`, `stalled`, `stall_threshold`, `inactive_threshold` returns zero matches outside the LastActivity-write site itself. The orchestrator (`implement-feature` Progress Loop) has no observable signal that a task claimed `IN_PROGRESS` 30 minutes ago has stopped emitting tool events.\\n\\nSymptom: a kage-bunshin or task-worker that hangs (model stuck in retry loop, deadlocked on missing input, network partition to MCP server) leaves the task `IN_PROGRESS` indefinitely. The dispatch loop cannot tell the difference between a task actively working and a task that has gone silent. The orchestrator must either wait the maximum allowed time or kill blindly.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d40db891b4b83621a6cd47262ce364ab28fd123266e060317efbd5c5069cfae5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtYrng\"}"}